    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2-a1">

                <pb facs="0114" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg6"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                        353.—Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moerser to Mr. Grant.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Krakau.</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-04-09"
                    >undated</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>My son, Charles Mercy, an American citizen, who has been living in America for
                    thirty years and fought in the Mexican war, came to Krakau to pay me a visit,
                    and yesterday, when on the point of leaving, he was arrested at the railway
                    depot by the police, who took from him 5,000 florins and put him into jail.
                    Requesting your protection, I ask what shall I do.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. F. Moerser.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
